  "name": "Mando and dulpod (Goan Konkani song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Mando is the slow, sentimental Konkani song-and-dance of Goan Catholic society, shaped in the nineteenth and early twentieth centuries from Portuguese-era salon music and local melody on themes of love, separation and social events; dulpod are the quick, light songs of everyday life that follow it. They are sung, often by mixed groups, to violin, guitar and the ghumot clay-pot drum, and are showcased at the Goa Mando Festival.",
